@@ -132,6 +132,7 @@ games:
     win_condition: "MATCH a movable object to a target on FIVE attributes simultaneously: x, y, scale, rotation, and sjmtdfxdrc (a 5th property). Source: tn36.py:2153 vklyonlcrw = (obj.x==tgt.x and obj.y==tgt.y and obj.scale==tgt.scale and obj.rotation==tgt.rotation and obj.sjmtdfxdrc==tgt.sjmtdfxdrc). L1 at reset: obj=(x30,y13,s1,r0,sj11) tgt=(x30,y33,s1,r0,sj11) -> ONLY y is wrong (move down 20). Internal state is readable: env._game.fdksqlmpki.bzirenxmrg.{htntnzkbzu(obj),aqszntqeae(tgt)}."
     solver: "PROGRAM-EDITOR mechanic (FULLY RE'd 2026-06-17). The object runs an N-slot MOVE-PROGRAM (vkuvtkaerv); each slot holds a command code (tn36.py:2171 okllwtboml: 0=settle,1=left,2=right,3=down,33=up,5/6/7/16=rotate,8/9=scale+/-,14/15/63=property). Step CSPOIQWER=4. TOOL PALETTE = a 6-BIT code editor per slot: bit b's toggle-button is at (slot_x, slot_y_top + 3*b) for b=0..5 (values 1,2,4,8,16,32), so ANY code = sum of its set bits (down 3=bit0+bit1; up 33=bit0+bit5; scale+ 8=bit3; rotate+90 5=bit0+bit2). Slot positions ARE READABLE (controller.pfyayhyovw[i].{x,y}) and RE-LAY-OUT per level (L1: 5 slots; L2: 4 slots; different x/y) -> DISCOVER, don't hardcode. RUN by clicking the object sub-button sxhtkytekm (center, discovered). L1: program [3,3,3,3,3]=5 downs->y13->33. L2: [33,33,33,33]=4 ups->y24->8."
     reproduce: "scripts/arc3_tn36_offline_solver.py — GENERAL from-scratch solver: reads obj/target deltas + the per-level button layout (pfyayhyovw), computes the move-program (down/up/left/right + scale/rotate), edits slots via bit-toggle clicks, runs, and CHAINS levels. Reproduces L1+L2 (reproduced=True claimed_level=2, 25 clicks). Frozen trajectory at results/arc_explore_trajectory_tn36.json. Property change (sjmtdfxdrc, codes 14/15/63) is the one transform not yet decoded — extend when a level needs it."
+    next: "L3 (obj 37,20 -> tgt 53,12; 6 slots) computes a valid position program [33,33,2,2,2,2] (2 ups+4 rights) but running it does NOT win under any move ORDER tried -> L3 has a deeper mechanic than pure position-delta (likely OBSTACLES/path-blocking via cwtesiybfx's collision revert, tn36.py:2269, or a wgzwawbgew checkpoint requirement). Next: instrument the per-move object position during an L3 run to see where a move is blocked, then route around it (the moves are right; the PATH is the gap)."
     action_model: "ACTION6 click; data schema IS {x,y} and display->grid is 1:1 (camera.display_to_grid(30,13)==(30,13)). Clicks register (121/121 change the grid). Control is a PROGRAM/transform EDITOR, not direct steering: dispatch (tn36.py:2500) routes a click to a tool-palette (miytdaqzei, EMPTY at reset) else mvqheosngn(apply/2nd-object) else bzirenxmrg(the object); the object carries a move-program vkuvtkaerv=[3,0,3,0,0]; clicking it runs mmmdksslmq()->olrpupaury(). The exact EDIT->EXECUTE semantics that drive obj.y 13->33 are not yet cracked (directly invoking mmmdksslmq did NOT move the object; palette empty)."
     gotchas:
       - "CORRECTION (2026-06-17, deep RE): the prior 'ACTION6 schema is NOT {x,y} / KeyError x / explorer ERRORED' note is STALE/WRONG. {x,y} works; the KeyError only fires for data=None. rich_action_candidates emits {x,y} and graph_explore_solve_v2 runs CLEAN on tn36 (no error) — it just NO-ADVANCEs because the win needs the program-editor mechanic, not blind clicks."
